Standards of Professionalism
Magistrate Jacobs expects all attorneys who appear to know and adhere to the Twelfth Judicial Circuit’s
Standards of Professionalism
, also available on the websites of the
Manatee County Bar Association
and the
Sarasota County Bar Association
.
A. Remote Appearance
All hearings, with the exception non-evidentiary hearings scheduled for 30 minutes or less, will be held in person.
Requests for a hearing by audio or audio-video technology or for remote testimony
must
be in writing in accordance with Rule 2.530, Fla. R. Gen. Prac. & Jud. Admin. A copy of the motion must be forwarded to the Court in addition to the parties.
Please note
: Pleadings filed with the Clerk of Court do not come to the attention of the Court unless accompanied by a Form A, Form C or are emailed to the office.
If a Zoom hearing is approved the Notice of Hearing must contain the correct Zoom credentials.
